WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
- No one knows why humans get motion sick.

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:03.660
I mean, we know what causes it:

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.630
it's the difference between
the motion that we see

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.950
and the motion that we feel.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:08.600
But why nausea?

00:00:08.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Why not a migraine or a
loss of bladder control?

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:12.990
There's a popular theory that says

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.190
it's because our brain
thinks we've been poisoned.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.440
Some toxins do mess with your balance.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.240
But that is just a theory.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:23.103
One scientist describes that theory
as not just unproven but untestable.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.560
Anyway, I'm with these reprobates,

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.331
and we've made a car that brings
video game lag into the real world.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.610
- It lands right on the hazards,

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:37.006
so for when we crash...
[laughing]

00:00:37.006 --> 00:00:39.431
- Oh, there's two.
I felt like I just did a magic trick.

00:00:39.431 --> 00:00:41.540
- It's upside down! [laughing]

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:42.548
- Really?

00:00:42.548 --> 00:00:44.798
[laughing]

00:00:45.735 --> 00:00:46.710
- So here's the plan.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.390
Inside this shrouded driving compartment...

00:00:49.390 --> 00:00:50.740
Are you okay in there?

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.760
It's just suddenly very bright for him.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.330
The driver can see the view
projected on this monitor,

00:00:56.330 --> 00:01:00.150
and that view is coming from this
front-facing camera just here.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:01.470
And that view can be delayed

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:03.350
as it runs through the
passenger seat computer,

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:04.940
and that can be by fractions of a second

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.510
or by a minute if we wanted to.

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:08.700
Right, you ready?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:09.700
- Yeah.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:10.324
God d--

00:01:10.324 --> 00:01:11.580
[chuckling]

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:12.810
- Right, Michael, are you ready?

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.646
- Ready is a relative term, Tom.

00:01:14.646 --> 00:01:17.430
- Okay, on minimum lag, here we go,

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:20.510
in three, two, one, go.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:21.930
- Oh no!

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:22.763
Oh!

00:01:22.763 --> 00:01:23.596
Woo!

00:01:23.596 --> 00:01:25.050
We're about to crash into the--

00:01:25.050 --> 00:01:27.210
- No, you got it. Just go slow.

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:28.300
Go right.

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.050
Hard right, hard right, hard right.

00:01:31.269 --> 00:01:32.651
[laughing]

00:01:32.651 --> 00:01:33.484
- Woo!

00:01:33.484 --> 00:01:36.730
- Now, we are not running a proper
double-blind scientific experiment here.

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.410
But, from our rough results,
here's what we found.

00:01:39.410 --> 00:01:42.870
If the view is only very slightly lagged,
the brain just copes with it.

00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:45.420
It's weird watching a
screen to pilot a car,

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.703
but it can be done.

00:01:46.703 --> 00:01:48.610
Oh, that is weird!

00:01:48.610 --> 00:01:50.568
- Stop, stop, stop, stop!

00:01:50.568 --> 00:01:51.401
Woo-hoo!

00:01:51.401 --> 00:01:53.100
- Where's the shifter?
Where's the shifter?

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.530
If the view is very lagged,
by more than a second,

00:01:55.530 --> 00:01:57.790
then the brain treats it
as two separate tasks,

00:01:57.790 --> 00:01:58.970
and it's like a logic puzzle.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:00.392
- Okay, okay.

00:02:00.392 --> 00:02:01.225
This is...

00:02:01.225 --> 00:02:04.270
This is actually, I think,
a little nauseating.

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:05.710
Oh my lord!

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:07.330
This is awful, Tom!

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.782
I have to go really slow.

00:02:08.782 --> 00:02:11.640
I don't know.
I actually, like, I don't feel sick.

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.970
I just feel, like, very confused.

00:02:13.970 --> 00:02:15.970
- You can drive and you
feel those reactions,

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:17.810
and you use the old view
to plot your course,

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.490
but the two are unrelated.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:21.440
It's a bit confusing and a
bit nauseating, but no more

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.860
than looking at any other
screen in a moving vehicle.

00:02:23.860 --> 00:02:26.880
Oh, I don't like this!
I don't like this at all!

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:27.713
- Stop, stop, stop, stop!

00:02:27.713 --> 00:02:28.702
[laughing]
- Really?

00:02:28.702 --> 00:02:30.910
[screaming]

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:32.350
That's so confusing!

00:02:32.350 --> 00:02:34.370
Like, in motion simulators
this is what you find.

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.810
You can trick the body, as long as
it's doing a little bit of movement,

00:02:36.810 --> 00:02:38.130
that it thinks
it's doing a lot.

00:02:38.130 --> 00:02:40.310
It turns out it works the other way.

00:02:40.310 --> 00:02:42.830
But there's this weird spot
between those two,

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:45.790
where the view is just lagged
by a fraction of a second,

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:47.930
enough that the brain
is trying to reconcile

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:51.560
the movement and the view
but failing constantly.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:54.253
And that, that is not pleasant.

00:02:55.396 --> 00:02:57.618
- Bro!
[laughing]

00:02:57.618 --> 00:02:58.451
Bro!

00:03:00.091 --> 00:03:01.070
Please!

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:01.913
Oh no!

00:03:03.105 --> 00:03:04.870
- Oh, this is so bad!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.680
- So I go over here.

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.180
So I'm in the future, right?

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.240
So that means I'm going too far right.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.260
Too far!

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.749
Awesome. I'm gonna go ahead and
vomit into that bucket if you don't mind.

00:03:15.749 --> 00:03:17.415
- How do you feel?

00:03:17.415 --> 00:03:20.670
- Oh my God!
That is the worst thing ever.

00:03:20.670 --> 00:03:21.730
- Oh!

00:03:21.730 --> 00:03:22.563
Oh!

00:03:23.508 --> 00:03:24.341
Oh.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.825
Oh yeah, this is an unpleasant experience.

00:03:30.825 --> 00:03:31.800
- Oh no!

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:33.130
Oh, I don't like this at all!

00:03:33.130 --> 00:03:33.980
- Okay.

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:37.093
Okay, go a little wider with this one.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:39.570
- Not wide enough!

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.030
- Stop, stop, stop, stop.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.341
Woop, there goes that cone.

00:03:42.341 --> 00:03:43.180
- Oh no!

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.228
[shouting] Now I'm nauseous.

00:03:44.228 --> 00:03:45.061
That's bad.

00:03:45.061 --> 00:03:46.020
- All right, Tom.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:46.970
- What was the time?

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:49.210
- You have officially the
worst time of the day.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:52.210
It's like two minutes and 30 seconds.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:53.933
- That's fair.
All right.

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:55.330
Let me... could someone please,

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.100
I'm gonna put the parking brake on
and keep my foot on the brake.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.960
Could someone please remove
the cone from under the car?

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.321
Thank you very much to William Osman
for partnering in building this with me.

00:04:04.321 --> 00:04:05.240
- Donating the car.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.000
- This was mostly you work and your car.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:07.870
Check out his channel for that.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.310
Thank you, Michael, for coming along.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.143
You can check out his channel

00:04:10.143 --> 00:04:12.480
for a lot of videos that
have been demonetized.

00:04:13.456 --> 00:04:14.380
Thank you, folks.

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:16.222
- We need to buy a buffing wheel.

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:17.658
[laughing]

00:04:17.658 --> 00:04:19.150
- It's gonna need more
than a buffing wheel.

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:19.983
- I'm sorry.

